namespace model {
/*! \page CD_intro Cluster Dynamics (CD)

\section CD_introduction Introduction

Cluster dynamics describes the point defects produced by irradiation and the loops they form.
It is one of the physics of the DefectiveCrystal, enabled by the name ClusterDynamics in the
<tt>physics</tt> line of DefectiveCrystal.txt, and it is solved on the finite-element mesh.

Two kinds of species are carried:

- mobile species (single vacancies, interstitials and small interstitial clusters), whose
  concentrations obey steady reaction-diffusion equations;
- immobile families (for zirconium, basal vacancy loops and three families of prismatic
  interstitial loops), each described by a number density and a defect content, which obey
  ordinary differential equations at each point.

The numbers of species are compile-time constants, set by the CMake options
<tt>MODELIB_CD_MSIZE</tt> and <tt>MODELIB_CD_ISIZE</tt>.

\section CD_classes Classes

- ClusterDynamics: the physics seen by the DefectiveCrystal. It applies the boundary conditions,
  calls the solvers, writes the fields, and converts the immobile fields to discrete loops.
- ClusterDynamicsParameters: the parameters read from the material file, and the reaction matrices.
- ClusterDynamicsFEM: the fields, their weak forms and the two solves of a step.
- SecondOrderReaction, FirstOrderReaction, LoopSinkReaction, VacancyLoopSource: the reaction and
  source terms of the mobile equations.
- ImmobileRateEquations: the rate equations of the immobile families at one point. It holds no
  finite-element type.
- ImmobileODESolver: the implicit integration of those equations at every node, by CVODE.
- ImmobileSinkRate, SpatialODESolver: the rates and their projection used by the explicit integrator.

\section CD_step One time step

-# Mobile species. ClusterDynamicsFEM::solveMobileClusters solves the steady equations by Newton
   iterations, for the immobile fields currently held. The immobile clusters enter through the
   sink LoopSinkReaction and through the vacancies they release, VacancyLoopSource.
-# Immobile families. ClusterDynamicsFEM::updateImmobileClusters advances them over the step with
   the mobile field held fixed. With <tt>immobileIntegrator=cvode</tt> (ClusterDynamics.txt),
   ImmobileODESolver integrates ImmobileRateEquations at each node: the equations are stiff, and
   independent from node to node. With <tt>immobileIntegrator=euler</tt>, the rates of
   ImmobileSinkRate are projected on the nodes and an explicit step is taken.

The two solves work on the same vectors of nodal values: nothing goes through a file.
The fields are written in the configuration files evl_n.txt at full precision, and a run that
finds such a file as evl_0.txt starts from its fields.

\section CD_equations Equations of the immobile families

For a family with n clusters per atom and c stored defects per atom,

\f[
\frac{dn}{dt} = \frac{s^{nuc}+G_L}{n^{nuc}} - a_n - \Delta N ,\qquad
\frac{dc}{dt} = \dot G^{c} + G_L + s^{nuc} - A_c - A^{emit} - \Delta C ,
\f]

with the content of the clusters born in cascades \f$G_L\f$ and from reactions between mobile
species \f$s^{nuc}\f$, the net absorption of mobile defects \f$\dot G^{c}\f$, the dissolution
\f$a_n\f$, \f$A_c\f$ and thermal emission \f$A^{emit}\f$ of the vacancy clusters, and the
coalescence \f$\Delta N\f$, \f$\Delta C\f$. Each term is a function of ImmobileRateEquations.
The model is that of the report docs/reports/GW_Phase4_D1M1.pdf.

\section CD_tutorials Tutorials and tests

- tutorials/spatialCDtest: growth strain of zirconium with constant loop densities (explicit integrator);
- tutorials/spatialCDcvode: nucleation, dissolution and coalescence of the loops (CVODE);
- simulations/run_simulation.ipynb: a grain of 200 nm to 10 dpa, with figures and a report;
- testsPy/clusterDynamics: the rate equations against an independent implementation, and the
  conversion to discrete loops.

*/
}
